  Here's a tip when watching games on NAO.  Use the uppercase letter
when selecting a game to watch and NAO will change the settings on your
TTY session to match the rows and columns of the game you're trying to
watch.  This is useful both for setting to strange rows and columns.
Just watch a game that's played at 80x24 to change back.

  Watching someone else play is fun all by itself.  Watching someone on
the Ascension Run while being on #nethack on freenode.org can be
exciting.  It's also interesting when someone asks for help on #nethack
and watching them play while reading the advice.


